<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Research AI Café #001 | JP"><section class="section"><div class="container prose"><div class="eyebrow">Research AI Café #001 | JP</div><h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4.7rem)">How are you using AI<br/>in your research?</h1><p class="lead">A Japanese-language roundtable on real AI practices among experimental researchers.</p><a class="event-poster" href="/images/research-ai-cafe-001-jp-poster.webp" aria-label="Open the Japanese poster at full size"><img src="/images/research-ai-cafe-001-jp-poster.webp" alt="Research AI Café #001 Japanese poster. Date, venue, and registration details are TBD." width="900" height="1274" /></a><div class="card event-facts"><strong>Date</strong><p>TBD</p><strong>Venue</strong><p>TBD</p><strong>Who</strong><p>Graduate students and early-career researchers, especially in experimental fields; all interested researchers are welcome.</p><strong>Language</strong><p>Japanese</p><strong>Fee</strong><p>Free</p></div><h2>Questions for this session</h2><ul><li>Where do you use AI in research?</li><li>What has been genuinely useful?</li><li>What has felt unsafe or unreliable?</li><li>What prevents you from using AI more effectively?</li><li>Who should we invite, and what should we ask next?</li></ul><h2>Planned format</h2><ul><li>Opening</li><li>Snapshot of current use</li><li>Lightning talk</li><li>Group discussion</li><li>Whole-group reflection</li><li>Informal conversation</li></ul><h2>Registration</h2><p>The registration form is being prepared.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
